Unapplied PHP Location redirect oracle

Base: 71255b1345d44e89a1f7208e58579b4c2ced5d0f
Base test blob: b4dd127f8095800db29d0333bbf660c4431d8f83
Status: preserved after the execution workspace disconnected. No production
implementation is included. The DSR baseline was launched, but no result was
recovered. The public module/runner JSON/SARIF cases have NOT been executed.
The cases were reviewed against native PHP header parameter and URL semantics;
PHP and the independent Node URL witnesses were not executed in this session.

39 source cases and an actual CLI policy/cache test extend the existing suite.
Rule/category names are proposed, not registered on main. Before activation,
run the oracle against the incumbent, implement bounded request/receiver flow,
add status/header lifetime controls, and run both native and public PHP suites.
In particular, an isolated response_code=200/201 is not a lasting safety proof:
later http_response_code or replacement headers can change the final response.
URL encoding and numeric conversion do not make a user-selected host safe.
Do not relax known unsafe cases, completeness gates, or public format checks.

Apply to the exact base with git apply --check, then git apply; this archival
file does not alter active scanner behavior or activate a failing test gate.

